<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zamora</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zamora is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douro">Douro</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and León, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, capital of the province of Zamora. Fortified by the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a> in 893, it was a key stronghold on the Christian frontier along the Douro and was besieged repeatedly in the following centuries. In 1143 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-zamora">Treaty of Zamora</a> saw Alfonso VII of León recognise <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-portugal">Afonso Henriques</a> as king of Portugal. Its Romanesque churches and cathedral are among the finest in Spain.</p></div>
